From: aiueo52 <aiueo52@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 08:52:02 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 109/121] GDN verify front: fork the MOVED combine gate after
 HC mix K0, qkvz on the alt stream

SGLANG_OPT_GDN_FRONT_OVERLAP=1 (default off) changes stream placement only:
- hc_norm_mix2 takes an after_normed hook, called right after the launch
  that completes normed; the attention HC's MOVED gate forks onto the GDN
  alt stream there and overlaps K1/K2.
- _forward_input_proj_direct puts qkvz on the alt stream and b/a on the
  main stream, so b/a's 3 CTAs are no longer starved behind the qkvz wave.
  Its existing join also joins the forked gate.
The fork is only offered when the layer will take the two-stream direct
projection (front_gate_stream), so every fork has a join inside the graph.

Microbench (fc-glue bench_gdn_front, graph replay): -3.6 us (M=4) and
-3.2 us (M=16) per GDN layer front; kernels and inputs are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
